{
  "FormatVersion": 3,
  "Id": "6010f3f0-c2cf-5f9e-a0ee-90c30aa2a0ff",
  "Description": "Six ragdolls fall onto a sphere. Each is ten bodies held by nine limited ball sockets.\n\nEvery body part is one [RigidBody] with a point per ragdoll, so ten nodes describe all six figures. Each [RigidJoint] then links part to part, figure by figure. SwingLimit keeps heads, elbows and knees from folding back.\n\nAKA: ragdoll, character, limbs, joint limits, swing limit\n\nTips\n- Change Count on [ScatterPointsInVolume] for more or fewer ragdolls; nothing else changes.\n- The parts are drawn as boxes scaled to each collider, straight from the world's buffer.\n- All parts share CollisionGroup 1, so limbs pass through each other and through other ragdolls.",
